data: {"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Animate elements entering viewport with inView\n\nSource: https://motion.dev/docs/inview\n\nDetects when elements matching a selector enter the viewport and animates them.\n\n```javascript\ninView(\"#carousel li\", (element) => {\n  animate(element, { opacity: 1 })\n})\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Animate span elements with stagger selector\n\nSource: https://motion.dev/docs/text-animation\n\nAnimates targeted child span elements sequentially using the animate function and stagger delay.\n\n```javascript\nimport { animate, stagger } from \"motion\"\n\nanimate(\n  \"h1 span\",\n  { opacity: 1 },\n  { delay: stagger(0.05) }\n)\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Stagger element animations with stagger in animateView\n\nSource: https://motion.dev/docs/animate-view\n\nStaggers enter, exit, or layout animations across multiple elements matched by a selector in .add(). Pass stagger() to the delay option to animate each element sequentially.\n\n```javascript\nimport { stagger } from \"motion\"\n\nanimateView(update)\n  .add(\".item\")\n  .enter(\n    { opacity: [0, 1], scale: [0.6, 1] },\n    { delay: stagger(0.05) }\n  )\n```"}]},"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":3}

